{
  "name": "Daily QA LinkedIn Post Agent created by Claude",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup checklist\n1. Credentials to attach: OpenAI, Google Gemini (PaLM) API, Google Sheets OAuth2, Telegram API, LinkedIn OAuth2.\n2. Create a Google Sheet called 'QA LinkedIn Post Log' with a tab 'Log' and header row: timestamp, topic, post_text, hashtags, image_prompt, status, notes, linkedin_post_id\n3. Put your Google Sheet's ID into every 'REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_SPREADSHEET_ID' field below.\n4. Put your Telegram chat_id into the two Telegram nodes.\n5. Verify the Google Gemini node's Operation is set to 'Generate an Image' after import — dropdown values can shift between n8n versions.\n6. LinkedIn's w_member_social scope needs app approval — apply for that first, it's the slowest step.\n7. Test with 'Execute Workflow' before activating the schedule.",
        "height": 528,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -208
      ],
      "id": "f727c787-1be6-42bb-84e6-cad79d3aee0b",
      "name": "Setup Notes"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "Additions beyond the original spec:\n\n1. TOPIC DEDUP: reads your log sheet first so the Research Agent avoids repeating a topic from the last ~30 posts.\n\n2. AUTO-DISCARD BEFORE HUMAN REVIEW: the Review Agent can reject a draft outright (e.g. factually shaky, off-tone) without wasting your time on a Telegram approval — you only get pinged for drafts that already passed an automated sanity check.\n\n3. RETRY LOOP: if a draft is auto-discarded OR you tap Disapprove, the workflow loops back and generates a brand-new topic/post/image rather than just giving up for the day.\n\n4. ATTEMPT CAP: retries are capped at 3 per day (based on how many Rejected/Auto-Discarded rows exist in today's log) — after that it sends one Telegram message saying it's pausing until tomorrow, instead of looping forever.\n\nEverything is logged to the sheet regardless of outcome, so you always have a full record.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 400,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        352
      ],
      "id": "c004a99d-e8c2-4581-90f7-4ba2dfff17ea",
      "name": "Enhancement Notes"
    },
    {
